```blockdiag
blockdiag {
  default_shape = roundedbox;
  user [shape = actor, label = "User"];
  lb [label = "Load Balancer"];
  check [shape = flowchart.condition, label = "Cached?"];
  db [shape = flowchart.database, label = "Database"];
  user -> lb -> check;
  check -> cache [label = "yes"];
  check -> app [label = "no"];
  app -> db;
  group {
    label = "Backend";
    app; cache;
  }
}
```

Each table is a block with `shape: sql_table` and one `column: type` per line. Constraints:
`id: int { constraint: primary_key }`, `foreign_key`, `unique`. Relationships connect columns:
`orders.user_id -> users.id`.

```d2
users: {
  shape: sql_table
  id: int { constraint: primary_key }
  email: varchar { constraint: unique }
}
orders: {
  shape: sql_table
  id: int { constraint: primary_key }
  user_id: int { constraint: foreign_key }
  total: decimal
}
orders.user_id -> users.id
```

Subgraphs whose name starts with `cluster` are drawn as boxes:
`subgraph cluster_backend { label="Backend"; api; worker; }`. Edges can cross clusters.

```dot
digraph Architecture {
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box, style=rounded];
  client [label="Browser"];
  subgraph cluster_backend {
    label="Backend";
    api [label="API Server"];
    worker [label="Worker"];
  }
  db [label="PostgreSQL", shape=cylinder];
  queue [label="Queue", shape=component];
  client -> api [label="HTTPS"];
  api -> db;
  api -> queue;
  queue -> worker;
  worker -> db;
}
```

Use `shape=diamond` for decisions and labelled edges for branches; `shape=oval` for start/end.

```dot
digraph Flow {
  node [shape=box];
  start [shape=oval, label="Start"];
  check [shape=diamond, label="Valid input?"];
  save [label="Save record"];
  err [label="Show error"];
  stop [shape=oval, label="End"];
  start -> check;
  check -> save [label="yes"];
  check -> err [label="no"];
  save -> stop;
  err -> check;
}
```

